The raw_region_map table maps the numeric codes to region names (01=WEST, 02=EAST, 03=NORTH, 04=SOUTH), and every code is unique and covers all four unexpected values. A fix is therefore determinable: decode the codes in silver_customers via a left join to the map, and keep the existing region values otherwise.

The join key is region_code as VARCHAR, so the leading zeros are preserved. Any region not in the map falls back to upper(region). Customers keep one row each because the map has unique codes.

{"diagnosis": "Some customers in raw_customers carry numeric region codes ('01'-'04') instead of names; raw_region_map provides an unambiguous one-to-one mapping to names, but silver_customers did not decode it.", "decision": "fix", "confidence": 0.9, "pre_sql": [], "step_overrides": {"silver_customers": "CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE silver_customers AS SELECT c.customer_id, COALESCE(upper(m.region_name), upper(c.region)) AS region FROM raw_customers c LEFT JOIN raw_region_map m ON c.region = m.region_code"}}
